window.docContents[233].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L1-___-Two-bodies--Synopsis--PKC-vocabulary-in-scope":{"contents":"New at this step:\n\n* SortOfSystem — the universal category of a system, here \"harmonic oscillator\".* Sorted (sortOf) — an object type whose objects know their sort.* Designated (designation, designation_inj) — an object type whose objects have distinct nominal names.* IndividualQuantity — a magnitude of kind k about one object o.* IndividualQuantity.add, IndividualQuantity.div — same-object, kind-licensed arithmetic.* DifferenceKind.ofScale — the difference law that licenses comparing two records of one quantity.* massK, springConstantK, omegaSquaredK — the oscillator's kinds; k/m has kind omegaSquaredK.\n\nCarried from earlier steps: Quantity, massQ, springQ.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L1 — Two bodies\u0009Synopsis","header":"5.2.1.2. PKC vocabulary in scope","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L1-___-Two-bodies--Synopsis--PKC-vocabulary-in-scope"}});